MELANIE WARRICK: Agreed.

00:25:53.850 --> 00:25:57.200
Well, Mark, how do I set up
SSL termination on Kubernetes

00:25:57.200 --> 00:25:58.760
with Let's Encrypt?

00:25:58.760 --> 00:26:01.880
MARK MANDEL: So I'm going to
defer to one of our teammates

00:26:01.880 --> 00:26:04.850
on it, who is a DPE who
works on Google Cloud.

00:26:04.850 --> 00:26:06.740
He has a really great
tutorial on GitHub

00:26:06.740 --> 00:26:08.735
for installing an open
source project called

00:26:08.735 --> 00:26:11.210
Cert Manager to get HTTPS
certificates from Let's

00:26:11.210 --> 00:26:11.720
Encrypt.

00:26:11.720 --> 00:26:13.470
If you're not familiar
with Let's Encrypt,

00:26:13.470 --> 00:26:14.930
it's basically a
free service that

00:26:14.930 --> 00:26:17.810
has programmatic APIs
for getting TLS and SSL

00:26:17.810 --> 00:26:19.260
certs, which is pretty awesome.

00:26:19.260 --> 00:26:19.640
And it's free.

00:26:19.640 --> 00:26:20.350
MELANIE WARRICK: Yes.

00:26:20.350 --> 00:26:21.320
MARK MANDEL: Which
is kind of amazing.

00:26:21.320 --> 00:26:22.340
It is worth noting--

00:26:22.340 --> 00:26:23.330
I find this confusing--

00:26:23.330 --> 00:26:24.950
I think a lot of
people use Cert Manager

00:26:24.950 --> 00:26:26.390
even though Cert
Manager says, hey,

00:26:26.390 --> 00:26:28.370
maybe be careful about
using this in production,

00:26:28.370 --> 00:26:29.720
because we don't know
if it's ready yet.

00:26:29.720 --> 00:26:31.860
But I know a lot of people that
use it, which is kind of fun.

00:26:31.860 --> 00:26:33.530
So I give you that
proviso as well.

00:26:33.530 --> 00:26:35.480
But the tutorial
also links to things

00:26:35.480 --> 00:26:37.230
like Cloudflare and
Backplane, like if you

00:26:37.230 --> 00:26:39.646
want to actually pay for a
service that's going to provide

00:26:39.646 --> 00:26:40.980
SSL certs for you as well.

00:26:40.980 --> 00:26:42.320
So there's a few
different options there.

00:26:42.320 --> 00:26:43.470
Yeah, Let's Encrypt
is pretty great.

00:26:43.470 --> 00:26:44.840
It's a great place to
get started and get

00:26:44.840 --> 00:26:45.840
playing with this stuff.

00:26:45.840 --> 00:26:47.841
So we'll link to that
article in the show notes.

00:26:47.841 --> 00:26:49.048
MELANIE WARRICK: Sounds good.

